								<img src="http://www.azamien.com/eq/froglip.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=708"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1047.msg10396#msg10396"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1047.msg10396#msg10396">Re: Omens of War - Will you Buy it?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #9 on:</b> August 23, 2004, 10:15:57 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I&#039;ll readily admit that I haven&#039;t done anything except sewers.&nbsp; However, that does not cloud my ability to label the expansion a steaming pile of shit.<br /><br />The AA&#039;s are, by and large, crap.<br /><br />The content was not finished upon release.&nbsp; Not just *the* endzone like in every expansion they&#039;ve released, but zones prior to the endzone were not finished for awhile either.<br /><br />Aside from not being finished, it was released with horrible encounter tuning.&nbsp; They admitted it was released for level 70 characters, but when that didn&#039;t make it into the expansion, they didn&#039;t even bother to go back and retune before taking our money.<br /><br />It added two utilities.&nbsp; (Afterall, expansions shouldn&#039;t just mean more zones.)&nbsp; One, the leadership abilities, are somewhat decent.&nbsp; The other, tribute, has been nerfed into uselessness when it wasn&#039;t even that great to begin with.<br /><br />No, my friend, it is not required that I raid every zone in an expansion for me to be able to label it a steaming pile of shit.&nbsp; It might be better after being retuned a bit, but at the time that I layed down my $30 or whatever it was, it was a joke.<br /><br />Thus, I would like one of the poll options to be &quot;I will wait and see if it&#039;s a steaming pile of shit like GoD was before I buy it.&quot;&nbsp; Pretty simple, really.<br /><br /><br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><div align="center"><br /><img src="http://www.azamien.com/eq/frogsig.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=817140" target="_blank">Frog Loots</a><br /></div>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
